join gertrude left
set {gertrude.spoke} += 1.0
gertrude: Oh! What are you doing in here?
- Looking for you.
	jump who
- Snooping.
	gertrude: Ehm. What?
	- Aren't you also snooping?
		gertrude: That is PREPOSTEROUS! I would never.
		- ?
			gertrude: Well. Maybe I would.
			- I thought so.
				gertrude: What are you snooping for?
				- Casper. I think he's hiding in here.
					gertrude: He's gone!
					gertrude: ...I already checked under the bed.
					- Oh.
						jump who
				- A buried chest. I was sent a treasure map in the mail.
					gertrude: How could there be buried chest on the second floor?
					- Um... I guess I don't know.
						jump who
				- You.
					gertrude: What?! Why possibly?
					if {kim.gertrude} == true:
						- You've lived here for ten years. I thought maybe you could fill me in on some background info.
							jump who
					else:
						- Um. I don't know.
							jump who
- What are YOU doing in here?
	jump who
label who
gertrude: Who on earth are you?
- A reporter.
	gertrude: Really! Well, here's my statement.
	gertrude: There's something suspicious about Matilda. Somebody should look into her.
	gertrude: And the background of that new husband of hers!
	set {gertrude.will} = true
	set {gertrude.matilda} = true
	gertrude: That's all I've got to say.
	leave --All--
	[end_timeline]
- A third-party witness for the will reading.
	gertrude: Well, I'm not sure how the will reading can go on without Casper here. It's a real shame. I wonder who they'll put in charge of the estate while they're both missing.
	- Who would be in the running?
		gertrude: Well, I've been living here and taking care of Casper here for 10 years, so...
		- I see.
			gertrude: Actually, I don't have time to be talking to you. Goodbye.
			[end_timeline]
leave --All--
